      <abstract>The First Congregational Church in Port Chester, New York, was gathered on June 25,
        1887. Rev. A. W. Lightbourne was the church's first minister. A building for the church was
        constructed in 1889. The church dissolved in 1915. The collection includes meeting minutes,
        ledgers, Sunday school records, and vital membership records.</abstract>
