        Describing Archives: A Content Standard.</p>
    </processinfo>
    <bioghist>
      <head>Historical Note</head>
      <p>The First Congregational Church in Port Chester, New York, was gathered on June 25, 1887. A
        Sunday school existed alongside the church. The church's first installed minister was Rev.
        A. W. Lightbourne. A Church was built along Westchester Avenue in 1889. The church dissolved
        in 1915. After the church's closure the building was sold to the North Baptist Church and
        the bell from the church was specifically gifted to the North Baptist Church.</p>
    </bioghist>
    <scopecontent>
      <head>Scope and Contents</head>
      <p>This collection contains administrative, social club, and membership related materials for
        the First Congregational Church in Port Chester, New York. The collection includes meeting
        minutes, ledgers, Sunday school records, and vital membership records.</p>
    </scopecontent>
    <arrangement>
      <head>Arrangement</head>
      <p>Materials in this collection have been arranged into chronological order by start date.</p>
    </arrangement>
